================================================================================
WHAT THE LICENCE ABOVE COVERS
================================================================================

The source code written for this project: everything under `app/src/`, the
build scripts in `tools/`, and the Gradle configuration.

It does not cover the artwork, fonts or data files described below. Those are
not mine to license, and including them here is not a claim that they are. They
are in the repository because this is a nostalgia project that recreates a
particular phone, and it cannot do that without them.

If you fork this, the code is yours to do as you like with. The rest is between
you and whoever owns it.


================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL IN THIS REPOSITORY
================================================================================

Fonts - app/src/main/res/font/
    segoeui_*.ttf and tahoma.ttf are Microsoft typefaces. Microsoft owns them
    and licenses them with Windows; they are neither mine to relicense nor
    covered by the MIT grant above.

Wallpapers - app/src/main/assets/wallpapers/
    The Lumia wallpapers that shipped with Windows Phone. Microsoft's.

Icons - app/src/main/assets/custom_icons_8/
    1,261 Metro-style SVG icons. The `appbar.*` file naming is that of the
    Modern UI Icons set by Austin Andrews (modernuiicons.com); this has not
    been verified against that project's terms, and anybody redistributing
    them should check rather than take this file's word for it.

Emoji list - app/src/main/assets/keyboard/emoji.txt
    Built by tools/emojibuild/build_emoji.py from Unicode's own
    emoji-test.txt. Subject to the Unicode Terms of Use,
    https://www.unicode.org/terms_of_use.html


================================================================================
THE WORD LISTS
================================================================================

Files:  app/src/main/assets/keyboard/en.trie
        app/src/main/assets/keyboard/en.bigrams

These are built by tools/dictbuild/ from word frequencies published by
hermitdave/FrequencyWords, which are themselves counted from the OpenSubtitles
corpus distributed through OPUS. Those frequency lists are licensed
CC BY-SA 3.0, so these files are offered on the same terms:

    Word frequencies from https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords
    (OpenSubtitles, via OPUS), licensed CC BY-SA 3.0.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

English, the only list that currently ships, is additionally filtered against
dwyl/english-words, which is public domain (Unlicense).

tools/dictbuild/ can build the other twenty-one languages, and filters those
against their Hunspell dictionaries from wooorm/dictionaries. Those dictionaries
are read on the machine running the build and are never committed here or
shipped in the app; their licences vary and six are GPL - Czech, German,
Italian, Macedonian, Norwegian and Ukrainian. tools/dictbuild/build_dict.py
names each one and its licence. Should those lists ever ship, they carry the
same CC BY-SA 3.0 attribution as English does, for the same reason.


================================================================================
DOWNLOADED AT RUNTIME, NOT DISTRIBUTED HERE
================================================================================

Speech models for on-device dictation are fetched from alphacephei.com when a
user first asks for offline dictation. They are Vosk's, under Apache 2.0, and
are not part of this repository or of the APK.
